  <h1>About Cuvolti</h1>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>This website shares knowledge and information — on whatever feels worth saying, whenever there's something worth writing. Whatever I want to write about, I write it and put it up here, without sticking to one fixed topic. Through it, my ideas, information, knowledge, and opinions reach anyone, anywhere in the world who wants to read them.</p>

  <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
  <p>This is an independent, one-person effort. I'm a commerce student, and alongside my studies, I spend much of my time building things — AI-driven content, small web projects, and now this. There's no newsroom, no editorial team, and no funding behind it. Every piece published here is written and put together by hand, in whatever time is left over after everything else.</p>

  <h2>The name, and what's next</h2>
  <p>Cuvolti was created from scratch — original, not borrowed or adapted from anything that already exists. It has no trademark filed and no domains such as cuvolti.com or cuvolti.in registered yet, simply because that kind of spending isn't something a student can afford right now. That is the only reason, not a strategic choice.</p>

  <p>The name stays open for that reason. If a brand or business ever sees something in it worth building on, that's a conversation worth having. Until then, this is what Cuvolti is: one person, writing, with room to grow into whatever it's meant to become.</p>
</div>
